cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Do Speed Cameras Make Chicago Safer? A Geospatial Causal Inference and Machine Learning Study"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible study of Chicago's automated speed enforcement program using
  matched difference-in-differences, conditional Poisson fixed effects, event
  studies, synthetic control and placebo tests, together with a separate
  LightGBM crash forecasting system with conformal prediction intervals.
